Z||000015||lennyb4||05-24-2000||09:01 AM||||Well i really dont care about this at all. BUT..I love to make fun of "RICERS" and thier little fart can imports, and i have some friends whos cars are the perfect example of this (i do it in front of thier face and they laugh just as much as i do)+ (they rag on fieros, corvettes, and other american cars just as much). Also if you took some time to look around you would find that there are forums for imports that rip our cars and taste as much as we do them. Its all in good humor. As for the handling issue my brother in law has a MR2. There was a oval track up here and we went for it. He was just as fast but couldnt hold a candle to my handling (my baby is all stock to). So just take a chill pill,relax and take it easy man..Like i said its all in good fun.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>P.S.<BR> Orge is one of the most knowledgeable people on this forum. He has helped me and other people ALOT with different problems.<p>[This message has been edited by lennyb4 (edited 05-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||WKDFIRO||05-24-2000||05:38 PM||||Another point to consider is that MR-2 are not built in a space frame configuration. Fieros have a STOUT B-pillar that pretty much acts as our center of structural integrity. No matter how much reenforcement I have seen on convertables they will always flex with out that pillar. MR-2 may have us in handling but the chassis is not as rigid as ours. The flip side is that is why we are so much heavier than they are. I beleive that the brace tower does help the MR-2s only because they inherently have flex in the chassis. As for rice bashing - well you can't bash them too much for having the technology to squeeze so much power out of almost nothing of displacement. <P>In many ways they share many things that muscle cars had from yesteryear. Cheap family cars, plentiful, easy to work on, a plethora of aftermarket parts. Just like a Chevy Nova from the 60s. Difference? Typical teenager today won't have the slightest idea how to rebuild a carb (its almost a lost art) but knows all about power chips and intakes. <P>Now the fart cans? Can't help them there. The way I look at it they are my competitors and it is wise to learn the ways of my adversary. ||||reg||6
